Provenance of the Go server
---------------------------

The Go implementation rooted at cmd/gobbonet/ and internal/ was written by
John McCardle and first published under the MIT licence:

    repository   https://github.com/jmccardle/gobbonet
    tag          mit-go-server   (commit 0b092f1, 22 August 2026)
    fork point   mit-fork        (commit bc40242, ElodineOfficial/gobbonet)

At the time it was written, ElodineOfficial/gobbonet was MIT-licensed; the
relicensing to AGPL-3.0 (commit 5a2f4f1) came afterwards, on 30 August 2026.

Of the Go source in the 1.7 release, 7,696 of 12,972 lines are byte-identical
to that MIT-licensed work. Twenty of the twenty-six files common to both trees
match at the blob level, as do go.mod and go.sum.

That work remains available from its author under the MIT licence at the
mit-go-server tag. Combining it here with AGPL-3.0 contributions means this
combined distribution is governed by the AGPL-3.0; it does not withdraw the
MIT grant on the original files, and it does not transfer their authorship.


